{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally and the Job Inquiry", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Breaking into the Field", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Consonant Blends - The <span class = \"italic\">spr</span> Sound", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Consonant clusters like <span class = \"italic\">/spr/</span>  can occur at the beginning of a word in English. <br/><br/>Practice blending the sound from one consonant into the next without adding a vowel in between.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Read the following words aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spring\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sprawl\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sprain\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spread\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spray\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sprint\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"springboard\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sprinkler\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I was sprinting towards the ball, but then I tripped in some mud and sprawled onto the field with my legs spread out like an eagle.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Now that it's spring, we play soccer outdoors.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Intonation in Long Questions  ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Intonation is important in statements and in long questions. You use the rise and fall of your voice to show the listener when you are or are not finished.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In long questions, the intonation falls and then rises to show the question is not finished. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Normally, you place an extra emphasis on some important verbs, adjectives and nouns in the question. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "At the end, the intonation rises or falls, depending on whether it is a yes/no or information question.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say these sentences. Place extra emphasis on the bolded words. Be sure to notice if the question is a yes/no or information question.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You don't <span class=\"strong\">think</span> that <span class=\"strong\">computers</span> help people <span class=\"strong\">connect</span> with each other?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you <span class=\"strong\">mean</span> you don't enjoy the <span class=\"strong\">time</span> you spend <span class=\"strong\">online</span>?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Don't you <span class=\"strong\">think</span> you should try to <span class=\"strong\">adapt</span> instead?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you think it is <span class=\"strong\">difficult</span> for someone who wants to <span class=\"strong\">start</span> working in journalism to <span class=\"strong\">break into</span> the field?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How <span class=\"strong\">challenging</span> do you think it is for a <span class=\"strong\">new</span> journalist it to find <span class=\"strong\">stories</span> that appeal to a <span class=\"strong\">wide</span> audience?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to sprawl", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stretch out in an unusual way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I tripped in some mud and sprawled onto the field.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about current events.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spring", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in North America,  the period of the year from March to June", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now that it's spring, we play soccer outdoors.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spread out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extended open, covering a large area (like open wings, arms or legs)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I tripped in some mud and fell onto the field with my legs spread out like an eagle.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to sprint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to run very quickly for a short time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was sprinting towards the ball when I tripped in some mud.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to trip", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to fall because of something on the ground", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I tripped in some mud as I was playing soccer. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "eagle", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a large predatory bird, often used as a symbol because of its wide wings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I sprawled onto the field with my legs spread out like an eagle.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to break into the field", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to start working in an area", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a new journalist, is it difficult to break into the field?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le15ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, choose a field of work, like acting in movies, business or medicine.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose roles. One person thinks it is easy to break into this field. The other person thinks it is difficult.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Before you start the role play, plan your ideas separately. Try to think of 3 - 4 reasons for your opinion. Do not talk about them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write key words to help you give your opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Complete the role play. Make sure you use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIn my opinion ...\u201d</span> or <span class=\"italic\">\u201cI don't think ...\u201d</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to keep the conversation going for 5 minutes.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write key words about a career field.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I engage in a role play about a career field.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use appropriate expressions to give my opinion.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can say and use the sound <span class=\"italic\">spr</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can use proper intonation in long questions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " 